{"name":"Tangerine Dream","hex":"#ff8449","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tangerine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slightly ovoid, orange-coloured  citrus fruit with a rough peel and a sour-sweet taste which is larger than a clementine and sometimes classed as a variety of mandarin orange.","A deep yellowish-orange colour, like that of a tangerine fruit."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a deep yellowish-orange colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tangerine"},{"term":"dream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping.","A hope or wish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see imaginary events in one's mind while sleeping.","To hope, to wish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tangerine Dream","blocks":[{"text":"Tangerine Dream is a German electronic music band founded in 1967 by Edgar Froese. The group has seen many personnel changes over the years, with Froese the only constant member until his death in January 2015. The best-known lineup of the group was its mid-1970s trio of Froese, Christopher Franke, and Peter Baumann. In 1979, Johannes Schmoelling replaced Baumann until his own departure in 1985. This lineup was notable for composing many movie soundtracks. Since Froese's death in 2015, the group has been under the leadership of Thorsten Quaeschning. Quaeschning is Froese's chosen successor and is currently the longest-serving band member, having joined in 2005. Quaeschning is currently joined by violinist Hoshiko Yamane who joined in 2011 and Paul Frick who joined in 2020. Prior to this Quaeschning and Yamane performed with Ulrich Schnauss from 2014 to 2020. Schnauss only played three shows with Froese in November 2014 before Froese's passing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Tangerine_Dream_live_at_The_Barbican_7th_Oct_2024_-_Phaedra_at_50_Tour_%2854052390691%29.jpg/330px-Tangerine_Dream_live_at_The_Barbican_7th_Oct_2024_-_Phaedra_at_50_Tour_%2854052390691%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tangerine_Dream"},{"title":"Tangerine Dream (Kaleidoscope album)","blocks":[{"text":"Tangerine Dream is Kaleidoscope's debut album released by Fontana Records on 24 November 1967. Despite the group’s following, good reviews and radio play it failed to reach the charts."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e3/KaleidoscopeTangerineDream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tangerine_Dream_(Kaleidoscope_album)"},{"title":"Tangerine","blocks":[{"text":"The tangerine is a type of citrus fruit that is orange in colour, that is considered either a variety of the mandarin orange, or a closely related species, under the name Citrus tangerina, or yet as a hybrid of mandarin orange varieties, with some pomelo contribution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/TangerineFruit.jpg/330px-TangerineFruit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tangerine"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/E-mu_Audity.jpg/330px-E-mu_Audity.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm